      "key": {
        "uuid": "33f79eed_5a9f9a2f",
        "filename": "Documentation/dev-contributing.txt",
        "patchSetId": 32
      },
      "lineNbr": 168,
      "author": {
        "id": 1006192
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-16T19:02:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e I don\u0027t believe this is accurate. For example, this prohibits cherry-picks\n\nHappy to add the exclusion of cherry-picks to other branches.\n\n\u003e and many other cases allowed under the CLA.\n\nI could not find the many other cases where the CLA accepts code where the contributor isn\u0027t the author. Do you have any reference?",
      "parentUuid": "dace9464_619662c6",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 166,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 168,
        "endChar": 24
      },
      "revId": "14e6c867b9d0cc90096f856fa7f38ec599738bf7",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "33a56ebb_d99a96e6",
        "filename": "Documentation/dev-contributing.txt",
        "patchSetId": 32
      },
      "lineNbr": 168,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002666
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-16T19:30:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e \u003e and many other cases allowed under the CLA.\n\u003e \n\u003e I could not find the many other cases where the CLA accepts code where the contributor isn\u0027t the author. Do you have any reference?\n\nIf you look at their definition of \"You\", it has this line:\n\u003e _For legal entities, the entity making a Contribution and all other entities that control, are controlled by, or are under common control with that entity are considered to be a single Contributor._\n\nSo, for purposes of the CLA, everyone at a company is the same contributor and anyone at that company can submit anyone else\u0027s code (because the company has the copyright).",
      "parentUuid": "33f79eed_5a9f9a2f",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 166,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 168,
        "endChar": 24
      },
      "revId": "14e6c867b9d0cc90096f856fa7f38ec599738bf7",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ac98d78b_ffd21120",
        "filename": "Documentation/dev-contributing.txt",
        "patchSetId": 32
      },
      "lineNbr": 168,
      "author": {
        "id": 1006192
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-19T07:21:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That is the company CLA: there are also individuals signing the CLA. Do you see any cases where an individual is authorized to upload someone else\u0027s code and claim authorship?",
      "parentUuid": "33a56ebb_d99a96e6",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 166,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 168,
        "endChar": 24
      },
      "revId": "14e6c867b9d0cc90096f856fa7f38ec599738bf7",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e68ca933_ebd46e32",
        "filename": "Documentation/dev-contributing.txt",
        "patchSetId": 32
      },
      "lineNbr": 168,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002666
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-19T21:14:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Do you see any cases where an individual is authorized to upload someone else\u0027s code and claim authorship?\n\nNo. However, I think that\u0027s irrelevant if it\u0027s allowed within the corp CLA as it means my original comment on this text being inaccurate is correct. If it\u0027s inaccurate for some contributors, then it\u0027s inaccurate.",
      "parentUuid": "ac98d78b_ffd21120",
      "range": {
