    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2668a122_e006be28",
        "filename": "Documentation/dev-contributing.txt",
        "patchSetId": 32
      },
      "lineNbr": 170,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002666
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-15T15:40:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This also has issues, for example with peer programming. The Author field cannot have more than one value, so it can never reflect the entirety of the contribution. I think we\u0027re still too close to legal definitions on this.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 169,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 170,
        "endChar": 73
      },
      "revId": "14e6c867b9d0cc90096f856fa7f38ec599738bf7",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ecfa48b1_255d1e5b",
        "filename": "Documentation/dev-contributing.txt",
        "patchSetId": 32
      },
      "lineNbr": 170,
      "author": {
        "id": 1006192
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-16T19:02:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We are referring to _attribution_ here, not the actual writing of the code, which can be done by humans or developers.\nWhen the code is partially derived from other changes, we also add the `Co-Authored-By` as a courtesy, but that doesn\u0027t mean that the author is exempt from knowing what the code does.\n\nDo you have any suggestions here?",
      "parentUuid": "2668a122_e006be28",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 169,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 170,
        "endChar": 73
      },
      "revId": "14e6c867b9d0cc90096f856fa7f38ec599738bf7",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2a8a81e4_adeb5c39",
        "filename": "Documentation/dev-contributing.txt",
        "patchSetId": 32
      },
      "lineNbr": 170,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002666
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-16T19:30:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Do you have any suggestions here?\n\nI would remove this whole section. The \"Human Attribution is Mandatory\" section above already covers the project guidelines we care to enforce. This section feels like unnecessary legalese text.",
      "parentUuid": "ecfa48b1_255d1e5b",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 169,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 170,
        "endChar": 73
      },
      "revId": "14e6c867b9d0cc90096f856fa7f38ec599738bf7",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "05b73e04_8f4c0c84",
        "filename": "Documentation/dev-contributing.txt",
        "patchSetId": 32
      },
      "lineNbr": 170,
      "author": {
        "id": 1006192
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-19T07:21:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Can you suggest a non-legalese form? We are stating that even if the code is partially or fully written by AI, the author field should continue to be assigned to the signer of the CLA (for individual contributors) or to an employee of the company signing the CLA (for company-wide CLAs).",
      "parentUuid": "2a8a81e4_adeb5c39",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 169,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 170,
        "endChar": 73
      },
      "revId": "14e6c867b9d0cc90096f856fa7f38ec599738bf7",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "31e7d604_bd7ba763",
        "filename": "Documentation/dev-contributing.txt",
        "patchSetId": 32
      },
      "lineNbr": 170,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002666
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-19T21:14:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e We are stating that even if the code is partially or fully written by AI, the author field should continue to be assigned to the signer of the CLA (for individual contributors) or to an employee of the company signing the CLA (for company-wide CLAs).\n\nAs I said in my last reply, that\u0027s already covered in the \"Human Attribution is Mandatory\" section above. I don\u0027t think we need to repeat it or further clarify it.\n\nThough I notice even there we have the \"The human submitting the change is the sole recognized responsible author of the code.\" text, which I think also goes contrary to the CLA terms, cherry-picks, etc.",
      "parentUuid": "05b73e04_8f4c0c84",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 169,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 170,
        "endChar": 73
      },
      "revId": "14e6c867b9d0cc90096f856fa7f38ec599738bf7",
