        "id": 1002666
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-15T15:40:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We could add that we encourage the use of AI to gain a better understanding of existing code.",
      "revId": "14e6c867b9d0cc90096f856fa7f38ec599738bf7",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "23c5c690_05640531",
        "filename": "Documentation/dev-contributing.txt",
        "patchSetId": 32
      },
      "lineNbr": 184,
      "author": {
        "id": 1006192
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-16T19:02:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Whatever is not explicitly forbidden is allowed, including the general use of AI for design extraction and reverse-engineering existing code.\n\nThere are many other uses of AI; I am wondering whether they are relevant to the \"contribution\" guidelines, though.",
      "parentUuid": "2ce58aae_e7189041",
      "revId": "14e6c867b9d0cc90096f856fa7f38ec599738bf7",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "07133223_5cb1d289",
        "filename": "Documentation/dev-contributing.txt",
        "patchSetId": 32
      },
      "lineNbr": 184,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002666
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-16T19:30:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Maybe not in this section, but the overall intent of this doc is to help contributors... contribute. It does not seem out of place to suggest a tool to improve how they could do that. I\u0027m thinking something similar to what the [git project has](https://github.com/git/git/blob/master/Documentation/SubmittingPatches#L589) that reads more as \"here are ways we recommend using AI that we think benefit our project\":\n```\nWe strongly recommend using AI tools carefully and responsibly.\n \nContributors would often benefit more from AI by using it to guide and\nhelp them step by step towards producing a solution by themselves\nrather than by asking for a full solution that they would then mostly\ncopy-paste. They can also use AI to help with debugging, or with\nchecking for obvious mistakes, things that can be improved, things\nthat don’t match our style, guidelines or our feedback, before sending\nit to us.\n```\n\nAnd as a note, I generally think our AI guidelines should be as short and simple as theirs, even if we\u0027re differing a bit the guidelines themselves.",
      "parentUuid": "23c5c690_05640531",
      "revId": "14e6c867b9d0cc90096f856fa7f38ec599738bf7",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
